SUMMARY:A Cosmologist's Guide To Life and Love
LOCATION:Edinburgh
DESCRIPTION:A multi-media mash up of comedy\, cosmology and chat. Dr Julian
  Mayers asks if studying the cosmos gives us any useful insight into life\,
  death and all those awkward moments in between on Earth? Down to earth\, a
 ccessible\, funny and ultimately uplifting\, he explores: parallel universe
 s\, how far you have to travel to find yourself in an infinite universe\, h
 ow you can time-travel\, why a physicist should speak at your funeral and d
 oes love exist out there in the cosmos. Laugh\, cry and go 'ooh that’s in
 teresting.' Sold out in 2024.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-at
 las/event/a-cosmologist-s-guide-to-life-and-love/
